ogic and error handling\'\np.level = 1\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Multiple trigger types and scheduling\'\np.level = 1\n\n# Slide 6: n8n Core Components\nslide = prs.slides.add_slide(slide_layout)\nslide.shapes.title.text = \'n8n Core Components for AI Agents\'\ncontent = slide.shapes.placeholders[1]\ntf = content.text_frame\ntf.text = \'Architecture Components:\'\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Triggers: Events that initiate workflows\'\np.level = 1\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Data Nodes: Fetch, transform, and process data\'\np.level = 1\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• AI Nodes: LLM integration for decision-making\'\np.level = 1\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Action Nodes: Execute tasks based on AI decisions\'\np.level = 1\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Control Nodes: Manage workflow logic and conditions\'\np.level = 1\n\n# Slide 7: Model Context Protocol Introduction\nslide = prs.slides.add_slide(slide_layout)\nslide.shapes.title.text = \'Model Context Protocol (MCP)\'\ncontent = slide.shapes.placeholders[1]\ntf = content.text_frame\ntf.text = \'What is MCP?\'\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Open standard by Anthropic (November 2024)\'\np.level = 1\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Standardizes AI-external system connections\'\np.level = 1\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Client-server architecture\'\np.level = 1\ntf.add_paragraph()\ntf.add_paragraph().text = \'Why MCP Matters:\'\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Eliminates fragmented integrations\'\np.level = 1\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Universal protocol for AI connections\'\np.level = 1\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'• Enables seamless data access\'\np.level = 1\n\n# Slide 8: MCP Architecture\nslide = prs.slides.add_slide(slide_layout)\nslide.shapes.title.text = \'MCP Architecture Components\'\ncontent = slide.shapes.placeholders[1]\ntf = content.text_frame\ntf.text = \'Three Key Components:\'\np = tf.add_paragraph()\np.text = \'